# Internationalization (i18n) Implementation

## Setup and Configuration

### i18n Configuration

The i18n setup is configured in [i18n.tsx](mdc:src/locales/i18n.tsx):
- Default language: Korean (`kr`)
- Available languages: Korean, English, Japanese
- Translation files: [kr.json](mdc:src/locales/kr.json), [en.json](mdc:src/locales/en.json), [ja.json](mdc:src/locales/ja.json)
- Already imported in [main.tsx](mdc:src/main.tsx)

## Translation File Structure

### Organize translations by feature/section in [kr.json](mdc:src/locales/kr.json):

```json
{
  "common": {
    "logo": "LOGO"
  },
  "navigation": {
    "features": "기능",
    "reviews": "고객 후기",
    "pricing": "가격 안내"
  },
  "auth": {
    "login": "로그인",
    "getStartedFree": "무료로 시작하기"
  },
  "hero": {
    "title": "학생들의 잃어버린 등불을 밝혀주세요",
    "description": "...",
    "ctaPrimary": "무료로 시작하기",
    "ctaSecondary": "기능 살펴보기"
  }
}
```

### Naming Conventions

- Use nested objects for logical grouping
- Use camelCase for keys
- Prefix by component type: `common.*`, `navigation.*`, `auth.*`, `hero.*`
- Use descriptive names: `ctaPrimary`, `ctaSecondary` instead of `button1`, `button2`

## Component Implementation Patterns

### Basic Pattern

```tsx
import React from 'react'
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next'

const ComponentName = () => {
  const { t } = useTranslation()

  return (
    <div>
      {t('section.key')}
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Static Data with Translations

Reference: [NavigationMenu.tsx](mdc:src/components/molecules/NavigationMenu.tsx)

```tsx
// ✅ Preferred: Call t() in data definition
const navigationItems = [
  { label: t('navigation.features'), href: '/features' },
  { label: t('navigation.reviews'), href: '/reviews' },
  { label: t('navigation.pricing'), href: '/pricing' },
]

// Then use directly in render
{navigationItems.map(item => (
  <a href={item.href}>{item.label}</a>
))}
```

### Complex Text with Line Breaks

Reference: [HeroSection.tsx](mdc:src/components/organisms/HeroSection.tsx)

```tsx
// For Korean text that may need word breaking
<h1 className="break-all">
  {t('hero.title')}
</h1>

// For long descriptions
<p>{t('hero.description')}</p>
```

### Nested Object Access

```tsx
// For nested translations
{t('hero.animationPlaceholder.title')}
{t('hero.animationPlaceholder.description')}
```

## Typography Considerations

### Korean Text Handling

- Add `break-all` class for Korean text that might overflow
- Korean text often needs more vertical space
- Consider line-height adjustments for Korean characters

```tsx
<h1 className="break-all leading-tight">
  {t('hero.title')}
</h1>
```

## Component-Specific Patterns

### Navigation Components

Reference: [NavigationMenu.tsx](mdc:src/components/molecules/NavigationMenu.tsx)

- Define navigation items inside component using translations
- Keep href values static, translate only labels
- Use consistent hover states with `hover:text-neutral-60`

### Button Components

Reference: [HeaderActions.tsx](mdc:src/components/molecules/HeaderActions.tsx)

- Wrap button text directly with `t()`
- Keep button styling separate from text content
- Use descriptive keys: `auth.login`, `auth.getStartedFree`

### Hero/Section Components

Reference: [HeroSection.tsx](mdc:src/components/organisms/HeroSection.tsx)

- Group related content: `hero.title`, `hero.description`, `hero.ctaPrimary`
- Use nested objects for complex content: `hero.animationPlaceholder.title`
- Consider responsive text sizing with breakpoints

## Best Practices

1. **Always use useTranslation hook** in functional components
2. **Group translations logically** by component/feature area
3. **Use descriptive key names** that indicate purpose
4. **Handle long Korean text** with appropriate CSS classes
5. **Keep static data** (URLs, IDs) separate from translatable content
6. **Call t() early** in component for static arrays/objects
7. **Test text overflow** especially for Korean content
8. **Maintain consistency** in naming conventions across translation files

## Common Gotchas

- Don't forget to import `useTranslation` from `'react-i18next'`
- Korean text may overflow in fixed-width containers - use `break-all`
- Always define the `t` function with `const { t } = useTranslation()`
- Test components with different language content lengths
